## What I Did

Mentored teams through six human-centered design projects in a 10-week course through hosting office hours 2-3x / week. Worked with professors and the Dartmouth Center for Advanced Learning to secure a $1,500 DCAL grant to design a generative AI design challenge adopted as the course final.
Led a 2-hour design thinking lecture in place of a professor's last-minute illness.
Led and faciliated a two 2-hour workshops on design thinking for 30+ students for students in other courses.

## What I Learned

Teaching design is itself a design problem: students need structure, room to experiment, and feedback specific enough to help them move forward. I also learned that good facilitation means staying adaptable, whether that means stepping in for an unexpected lecture, supporting teams through office hours, or turning an emerging technology into a rigorous, hands-on course challenge.


